  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["Q1", "R5", "JP1", "J2"],
      "pins": ["Q1.1", "Q1.3", "J2.1", "J2.4", "JP1.2"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "GND", "PWM_OUT", "Q_PWM5_GSD"],
      "observed": "Q1 (the P‑FET next to Q2/BC817) has two of its terminals tied straight to the supply rails: one lead to the green VCC net (same node as JP1 pin2 / U2‑8 / R1 top) and the other lead to the GND net (same node as J2 pin1 / C1 bottom). Its third lead is the gate, on Q_PWM5_GSD, pulled up by R1 to VCC and pulled down by Q2. The fan PWM line J2.4 (PWM_OUT) is instead connected only through R5 to the MCU PWM net, so Q1's switched terminal is not in the PWM_OUT path.",
      "expected": "Q1 should be the high/low‑side switch that drives the fan PWM line: its gate on Q_PWM5_GSD, one terminal on a rail and the other on PWM_OUT (the fan PWM input), so it level‑shifts/switches the fan control signal. No FET terminal should sit on both VCC and GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet / (fan_controller.kicad_sch): Q1 drawn with leads to 'VCC' (green wire from JP1 pin 2, also into U2 pin 8 and R1 top) and to 'GND' (wire from J2 pin 1); gate lead on net 'Q_PWM5_GSD' shared with R1 bottom and Q2 pin 1."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet /: J2 FAN pin 4 'PWM_OUT' -> R5 (1K) -> 'PWM' net; PWM_OUT is not connected to Q1."}
      ],
      "impact": "When Q2 pulls Q_PWM5_GSD low (or high, depending on Q1's type) Q1 turns on and directly shorts VCC to GND, blowing the supply/regulator or latch‑up; meanwhile the fan PWM input is driven only by the MCU's 5 V logic through R5, so the intended level‑shifted PWM control of the fan is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing shows Q1 wired with two terminals directly across the VCC and GND rails (gate on Q_PWM5_GSD) while the fan PWM line PWM_OUT is bypassed via R5 to the MCU PWM net; this misconnection both shorts the supply when Q1 conducts and removes the intended fan‑PWM switching, so I report one anomaly."
}

